From 562804a4c897d3bcef217207f3efb8c7713e6d3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ogdanimal <306057786+ogdanimal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:16:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Sample counts 2 and 8 where the adapter supports them

IsSupportedSampleCount adds 2 and 8 to WebGPU's 1 and 4 for textures, render pipelines and render
bundles when PhysicalDeviceBase::SupportsExtraSampleCount says the adapter renders and resolves them
on its colour and depth formats: Vulkan's framebuffer colour and depth sample counts, D3D12's
multisample quality levels, Metal's supportsTextureSampleCount, GL's texture sample limits. Others
keep 1 and 4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RjydsaTAV42JRd8fVw2QCA
